-## 💥 HTML-to-PowerPoint Magic
+## 📊 Streaming table pagination
 
-Convert any HTML `<table>` into fully formatted PowerPoint slides - automatically and effortlessly.
+v5 removes the legacy DOM-capture API. Convert HTML or other application data
+to typed `TableRow` values in your own adapter, then pass those rows to the
+streaming session:
 
 ```javascript
-let pptx = new pptxgen();
-pptx.tableToSlides("tableElementId");
-pptx.writeFile({ fileName: "html2pptx-demo.pptx" });
+const pptx = new PptxGenJS();
+const session = await pptx.beginStreaming({ destination });
+
+await session.tableToSlides([
+  [
+    { text: "Name", options: { bold: true } },
+    { text: "Value", options: { bold: true } },
+  ],
+  [
+    { text: "Alpha" },
+    { text: "42" },
+  ],
+], {
+  x: 0.5,
+  y: 0.5,
+  w: 9,
+  h: 4.5,
+  autoPage: true,
+});
+
+await session.finalize();
 ```
 
-Perfect for transforming:
-
-- Dynamic dashboards and data reports
-- Exportable grids in web apps
-- Tabular content from CMS or BI tools
-
-[View Full Docs & Live Demo](https://gitbrent.github.io/PptxGenJS/html2pptx/)
+This keeps DOM measurement and application-specific HTML parsing outside the
+core package while retaining typed cells, colspan support, and bounded
+forward-only pagination.
 
